---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import ToggleGroupDemo from "../../components/ToggleGroupDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Toggle Group"
  description="A row or column of toggle buttons that share one value, for view switches, filters, and text styles."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Toggle Group</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Toggle buttons that share one value. Use it to pick a layout, a time range,
    or a theme, or to turn several text styles on at once.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ToggleGroupDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Toggle group usage"
      code={`import { ToggleGroup, ToggleGroupItem } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/toggle-group";

const [range, setRange] = useState(30);

<ToggleGroup
  aria-label="Time range"
  variant="outline"
  size="sm"
  spacing={0}
  value={[String(range)]}
  onValueChange={(value) => {
    // Keep one choice: ignore a press that would clear it.
    if (value[0]) setRange(Number(value[0]));
  }}
>
  <ToggleGroupItem value="7">7d</ToggleGroupItem>
  <ToggleGroupItem value="30">30d</ToggleGroupItem>
</ToggleGroup>

<ToggleGroup aria-label="Text style" multiple defaultValue={["bold"]}>
  <ToggleGroupItem value="bold" aria-label="Bold"><Bold /></ToggleGroupItem>
  <ToggleGroupItem value="italic" aria-label="Italic"><Italic /></ToggleGroupItem>
</ToggleGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      The value is always an array of item values. Pass <code>value</code> and
      <code>onValueChange</code> to control it, or <code>defaultValue</code>.
      Without <code>multiple</code>, pressing an item releases the others, and
      pressing the active item again sends an empty array. Ignore an empty
      array, as above, when one choice must stay selected. Give
      <code>ToggleGroup</code> a type, as in <code
        >{"<ToggleGroup<Layout>>"}</code
      >, to type the values.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> is <code>"default"</code> (no border) or <code
        >"outline"</code
      > (a control border on each item). <code>size</code> is <code>"sm"</code>
      (28px, 12px text), <code>"default"</code> (32px), or <code>"lg"</code> (36px).
      Items inherit both from the group.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>spacing</code> is the gap between items in 4px steps and defaults to <code
        >2</code
      > (8px). <code>spacing={"{0}"}</code> joins the items into one segmented control:
      inner corners are square and outline items share one border. <code
        >orientation</code
      > is <code>"horizontal"</code> (default) or <code>"vertical"</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> on the group disables every item; on an item it disables
      only that item. Icons are 16px (14px in <code>sm</code>) unless they set
      their own size. Mark a leading or trailing icon with <code
        >data-icon="inline-start"</code
      > or <code>"inline-end"</code> to tighten padding. Both parts take Base UI props
      such as <code>render</code>, <code>loopFocus</code>, and state functions
      for <code>className</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The group renders <code>role="group"</code>; name it with <code
        >aria-label</code
      >. Each item is a button with <code>aria-pressed</code>. Tab moves into
      the group once. Left and Right arrows (Up and Down when vertical) move
      between items and loop at the ends; Home and End jump to the first and
      last. Space or Enter presses the focused item. Disabled items are skipped.
      An icon-only item needs its own <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
    <p>Color changes take 120ms and stop when reduced motion is requested.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Pressed items use <code>--sprout-primary-subtle</code> and <code
        >--sprout-primary</code
      >, so the TulipFarm theme tints them green. Idle items use <code
        >--sprout-muted</code
      >, hover uses <code>--sprout-hover</code>, outline borders use <code
        >--sprout-input</code
      >, and the focus ring uses <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
